<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dinh Phe De</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">974–1001</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Dinh Toan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dinh Phe De, born Dinh Toan, was the second and last emperor of the Dinh dynasty in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, put on the throne as a child after his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinh-tien-hoang">Dinh Tien Hoang</a> was murdered in 979. Facing a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> invasion, the court and his mother made the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh">Le Hoan</a> emperor in 980, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-le-dynasty">Early Le dynasty</a>. He was killed in 1001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dinh-phe-de.jpg" alt="Dinh Phe De" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kien1980v at Vietnamese Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dinhtoan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
